BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mamma Mia! Singalong
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260610
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260611
DTSTAMP:20260611T093549Z
UID:019dd527-86ab-9169-d6d5-423d5bb36ee0@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Selected by the Actors Branch\n\nWednesday\, June 10\, 2026\n\
 nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 48m\n\n2008 | 
 108 min. | USA | Color | English/Greek | Rated PG-13 | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: 
 Phyllida Lloyd \nWRITTEN BY: Catherine Johnson \nWITH: Meryl Streep\, Pier
 ce Brosnan\, Colin Firth\, Stellan Skarsgård\n\nType: Screenings\n\nA you
 ng woman plans her wedding at the Greek island hotel of her free-spirited 
 mother\, not revealing that she has invited three of her mom’s former lo
 vers in an attempt to identify her biological father. Phyllida Lloyd (The 
 Iron Lady\, 2011) made her feature directing debut with this lively film v
 ersion of the blockbuster Broadway musical\, which incorporates the hit so
 ngs of the Swedish group ABBA. The all-star international cast is led by M
 eryl Streep and Amanda Seyfried as mother and daughter\, with Christine Ba
 ranski and Julie Walters as Streep’s former bandmates and Pierce Brosnan
 \, Colin Firth and Stellan Skarsgård as the possible fathers. The song sc
 ore includes such pop classics as “Dancing Queen\,” “Waterloo” and
  the title number. \nLyrics will appear on screen during the songs. Audien
 ce participation strongly encouraged.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/mama-mia-019dd527-86a
 b-9169-d6d5-423d5bb36ee0
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Grave of the Fireflies
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260610
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260611
DTSTAMP:20260611T093549Z
UID:019dd4e0-8733-3af6-b256-65564b3fef42@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Wednesday\, June 10\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Moti
 on Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 29m\n\n1988 | 89 min. | Japan | Color | Japanes
 e with English subtitles | Not Rated | DCP\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Isao Taka
 hata \nWITH: Tsutomu Tatsumi\, Ayano Shiraishi\, Yoshiko Shinohara\, Akem
 i Yamaguchi\n\nType: Screenings\n\nDirector Isao Takahata’s first film f
 or Studio Ghibli is a harrowing depiction of the last days of World War II
  as seen through the eyes of teenager Seita and his little sister Setsuko.
  After Allied firebombing destroys their home\, family\, and much of Kobe 
 city\, the two must fend for themselves and search for joy in their war-to
 rn community. Based on Nosaka Akiyuki’s semi-autobiographical account of
  the same name\, Grave of the Fireflies is an uncompromising portrait of p
 ersonal tragedy and loss of innocence in war.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/grave-of-the-fireflie
 s-019dd4e0-8733-3af6-b256-65564b3fef42
END:VEVENT
