BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gentlemen Prefer Blondes with Monkey Business in 4K
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T213000
DTSTAMP:20260611T093549Z
UID:019dda5a-ab50-7efe-4f00-64859f98521f@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, June 12\, 2026 at 6:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum
  of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 31m\n\n1953 | 91 min. | USA | Technicol
 or | English | Not Rated | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Howard Hawks  \nWRITTEN BY
 : Charles Lederer  \nWITH: Jane Russell\, Marilyn Monroe\, Charles Coburn
 \, Elliott Reid\n\nType: Screenings\n\nGentlemen Prefer Blondes In this 19
 53 musical comedy\, adapted from Joseph Fields and Anita Loos’s searingl
 y funny stage musical based on her 1925 novella\, showgirl Lorelei (Marily
 n Monroe) is resplendent in beautiful gowns\, most notably in the pink sat
 in dress designed by Travilla during the now-classic number “Diamonds Ar
 e a Girl’s Best Friend.” Lorelei is seen throughout the picture in jew
 el tones and literal jewels\, carefully selected to play up the lush Techn
 icolor cinematography lensed by Harry J. Wild. Both effervescent and timel
 ess\, this witty gem showcases Monroe’s brilliant comic timing as well a
 s her vocal chops. Premiering in the middle of the actress’s career and 
 released the same year as Niagara and How to Marry a Millionaire\, Howard 
 Hawks’s film helped to plant Monroe in the hearts of the American public
 \, making her one of the most famous people in the US.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/gentlemen-prefer-blon
 des-with-monkey-business-019dda5a-ab50-7efe-4f00-64859f98521f
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Michael Mann’s Manhunter: The Final Cut with Michael Mann
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T213000
DTSTAMP:20260611T093549Z
UID:019dd53d-50af-baad-9b14-3838732fe7b0@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: writer and director Michael Mann\n\nFriday\, June 1
 2\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRunt
 ime: 2h\n\n1986 | 120 min. | USA | Color | Scope | English | Rated R | 4K 
 DCP \nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Michael Mann \nWITH: William Petersen\, Kim Gre
 ist\, Joan Allen\, Tom Noonan\n\nType: Screenings\n\nA retired criminal pr
 ofiler (William Petersen) reluctantly returns to the FBI to help track dow
 n a serial killer of families and is forced to consult an expert—the imp
 risoned Dr. Hannibal Lecktor (Brian Cox in a subtly chilling performance).
  The third feature written and directed by Michael Mann is a gripping adap
 tation of the first of Thomas Harris’s four novels featuring the iconic 
 murderer\, and benefits from the filmmaker’s typically striking visuals 
 as well as a top-notch supporting cast\, including Tom Noonan as the hunte
 d killer\, and three-time Oscar nominee Joan Allen (The Contender\, 2000) 
 as his blind love interest.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/manhunter-the-final-c
 ut-with-michael-mann-019dd53d-50af-baad-9b14-3838732fe7b0
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Escape to Witch Mountain
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T121500
DTSTAMP:20260611T093549Z
UID:019db0ff-6d56-f857-758e-f7b7876d325b@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, June 13\, 2026 at 11 am\n\nLocation: Academy Museum
  of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 37m\n\n1975 | 97 min. | USA | Color | E
 nglish | Rated G | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: John Hough \nWRTTEN BY: Robert Malco
 lm Young \nWITH: Eddie Albert\, Ray Milland\, Donald Pleasence\, Kim Richa
 rds\n\nType: Screenings\n\nDisney produced this initial chapter of its Wit
 ch Mountain series during its Dark Age. It follows two orphaned siblings\,
  Tony and Tia\, who possess mysterious psychic powers\; Tony can move obje
 cts with his harmonica\, while Tia can communicate telepathically and mani
 fest premonition. When the evil\, wealthy Aristotle Bolt\, and his employe
 e\, Lucas Deranian\, learn about these enigmatic traits\, they plan a wick
 ed scheme to kidnap the siblings. Against the lush greenery of valleys and
  beautiful ocean\, Tony and Tia’s dangerous escape from Bolt turns into 
 a charming\, endearing adventure when Jason O’Day\, a widower camper\, j
 oins them in search of a place indicated on a map hidden in Tia’s star c
 ase\, an item she carries with her at all times.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/escape-to-witch-mount
 ain-019db0ff-6d56-f857-758e-f7b7876d325b
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ladies of the Chorus in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T160000
DTSTAMP:20260611T093549Z
UID:019dda5e-977f-fb03-d37f-5861011de57b@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, June 13\, 2026 at 3 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum 
 of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 1m\n\n1948 | 61 min | USA | Black-and-Wh
 ite | English | Not Rated | 35mm \nDIRECTED BY: Phil Karlson \nWRITTEN B
 Y: Harry Sauber\, Joseph Carole \nWITH: Marilyn Monroe\, Adele Jergens\, 
 Rand Brooks\, Nana Bryant\n\nType: Screenings\n\nPeggy Martin (Marilyn Mon
 roe)\, a burlesque-show chorus girl who works alongside her mother\, Mae (
 Adele Jergens)\, gets her big break after the lead unexpectedly quits. Whe
 n Peggy is pursued by the wealthy society man\, Randy Carroll (Rand Brooks
 )\, Mae worries their class differences will doom the relationship and tri
 es to protect Peggy from the same heartbreak she once suffered. Ladies of 
 the Chorus features Marilyn’s first starring role\, and her only film ro
 le during her short stint on contract at Columbia Pictures. The film also 
 marked the first time Monroe sang and danced in a film.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/ladies-of-the-chorus-
 019dda5e-977f-fb03-d37f-5861011de57b
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bound
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T223000
DTSTAMP:20260611T093549Z
UID:019dd53f-4f70-3abb-8859-66300caa3899@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, June 13\, 2026 at 7 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum 
 of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 45m\n\n1996 | 105 min. | USA | Color | E
 nglish | Rated R | DCP\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: The Wachowskis\nWITH: Jennife
 r Tilly\, Gina Gershon\, Joe Pantoliano\, John P. Ryan\n\nType: Screenings
 \n\nFresh out of prison and wanting to lay low\, Corky (Gina Gershon)\, ta
 kes a job fixing up an old apartment only to be seduced by Violet (Jennife
 r Tilly)\, the high-femme girl next door. As their secret affair heats up\
 , they devise a plan to steal $2 million from Violet’s mobster boyfriend
 . In the Wachowskis’ feature-film directorial debut\, they subvert tradi
 tional gender roles and genre convention\, allowing Corky and Violet to be
  deeply human as they navigate the boxes society creates for them and take
  down the oppressive men in their lives. After the Wachowskis refused stud
 io suggestions of changing Corky to a man\, they secured financing from Di
 no De Laurentiis\, who supported their original vision and added feminist 
 writer Susie Bright as a lesbian sex consultant to create what has now bec
 ome a cult classic in queer cinema.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/bound-019dd53f-4f70-3
 abb-8859-66300caa3899
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:How to Marry a Millionaire
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T223000
DTSTAMP:20260611T093549Z
UID:019dda67-f97f-c6c8-221a-626c11fa6abd@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, June 13\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Muse
 um of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 35m\n\n1953 | 95 min | USA | Technico
 lor | English | Not Rated | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Jean Negulesco \nWRITTEN 
 BY: Nunnally Johnson \nWITH: Betty Grable\, Marilyn Monroe\, Lauren Bacal
 l\, David Wayne\n\nType: Screenings\n\nSchatze\, Pola\, and Loco (Lauren B
 acall\, Marilyn Monroe\, Betty Grable) are Manhattan models on a mission t
 o marry rich husbands. Although they set their sights on Vanderbilts and R
 ockefellers\, their plans go awry when they become attracted to men who lo
 ok to be penniless. How to Marry a Millionaire was released at the end of 
 Monroe’s breakout year\, having starred in Gentlemen Prefer Blondes and 
 Niagara in 1953. The film is notable as the first to be completed in Cinem
 aScope\, and Monroe had such broad appeal that 20th Century-Fox used her t
 o advertise this new widescreen format: a slogan above an image of Marilyn
  claimed she was “Big as life and a million times more fun in Cinemascop
 e!”
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/how-to-marry-a-millio
 naire-019dda67-f97f-c6c8-221a-626c11fa6abd
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bend It Like Beckham in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T164500
DTSTAMP:20260611T093549Z
UID:019de534-a9ce-c7f9-7cea-8357cbbf429a@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, June 14\, 2026 at 11 am\n\nLocation: Academy Museum o
 f Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 52m\n\n2002 | 112 min. | UK/Germany/USA |
  Color | English | Rated PG-13 | 35mm  \nDIRECTED BY: Gurinder Chadha \n
 WRITTEN BY: Gurinder Chadha\, Guljit Bindra\, Paul Mayeda Berges \nWITH: 
 Parminder Nagra\, Keira Knightley\, Jonathan Rhys Meyers\, Anupam Kher\n\n
 Type: Screenings\n\nJesminder “Jess” Bhamra (Parminder Nagra) dreams o
 f playing professional soccer\, but her strict Sikh parents have designs o
 n her future as a lawyer and wife. So when Jess is recruited to join the l
 ocal amateur team by the confident Jules (Keira Knightley)\, Jess keeps th
 e hobby from her family\, until a publicized match forces her father to re
 ckon with his daughter’s true passion. Named for a kick technique popula
 rized by English soccer star David Beckham\, this British comedy was a cri
 tical success that inspired a generation of women to take up the sport.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/bend-it-like-beckham-
 019de534-a9ce-c7f9-7cea-8357cbbf429a
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Shaolin Soccer in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T153000
DTSTAMP:20260611T093549Z
UID:019de536-3069-56db-33cf-a0f9f32f6717@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, June 14\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum
  of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 27m\n\n2001 | 87 min. | Hong Kong | Col
 or | English dubbed | Rated PG-13 | 35mm \nDIRECTED BY: Stephen Chow \nWR
 ITTEN BY: Stephen Chow\, Tsang Kan-cheung \nWITH: Stephen Chow\, Vicki Zh
 ao\, Ng Man-tat\, Wong Yat-fei \n35mm print courtesy of Paramount Pictures
  Archive.\n\nType: Screenings\n\nSing (Stephen Chow)\, a former Shaolin mo
 nk known as Mighty Steel Leg\, is down on his luck. Poor and unable to rec
 ruit students to carry out his dream of popularizing martial arts in the m
 odern world\, he resorts to petty theft to survive. When former soccer pla
 yer Golden Leg Fung (longtime Chow collaborator Ng Man-tat) whose dreams o
 f stardom were squashed years prior\, notices Sing’s superhuman abilitie
 s\, he persuades him to use his skills for soccer. Sing assembles a team o
 f martial-arts masters to face off against a colorful swath of eccentric p
 rofessional players. Stephen Chow’s slapstick sports comedy was a smash 
 hit in Hong Kong and introduced Chow’s signature style to an internation
 al audience.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/shaolin-soccer-019de5
 36-3069-56db-33cf-a0f9f32f6717
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Offside in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T193000
DTSTAMP:20260611T093549Z
UID:019de537-5c7e-d4ab-fcac-842733f8eb3d@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, June 14\, 2026 at 5 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of
  Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 33m\n\n2006 | 93 min. | Iran | Color | Per
 sian | Rated PG | 35mm.  \nDIRECTED BY: Jafar Panahi \nWRITTEN BY: Jafar
  Panahi\, Shadmehr Rastin \nWITH: Sima Mobarak Shahi\, Safar Samandar\, S
 hayesteh Irani\, M. Kheyrabadi\n\nType: Screenings\n\nSince 1979\, women i
 n Iran have been barred from attending male sporting events\, though intre
 pid female fans often disguise themselves as men to gain access. After his
  daughter tried the same on multiple occasions\, filmmaker Jafar Panahi co
 -wrote this narrativized account of young women who attempt to sneak into 
 the June 2005 Iran/Bahrain FIFA World Cup-qualifying match in Tehran. Osca
 r-nominated screenwriter Panahi uses the backdrop of the actual 2005 game 
 to underscore the overwhelming male presence in public spaces and the ineq
 uality faced by women in 2006—a reality still pervasive 20 years later
 —as well as the value of community solidarity in the face of oppressive 
 regulations on the populace.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/offside-019de537-5c7e
 -d4ab-fcac-842733f8eb3d
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Only Yesterday
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260615T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260615T150000
DTSTAMP:20260611T093549Z
UID:019dd4e5-382b-1b21-6b82-7f190efce69f@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, June 15\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum
  of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 58m\n\n1991 | 118 min. | Japan | Color 
 | Japanese with English subtitles | Rated PG | DCP\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: I
 sao Takahata \nWITH: Miki Imai\, Toshiro Yanagiba\, Yoko Honna\, Michie T
 erada\n\nType: Screenings\n\nBased on the manga of the same name\, Isao Ta
 kahata’s second feature for Studio Ghibli is a serene memory piece featu
 ring 27-year-old Taeko reminiscing about her 1960s childhood\, travelling 
 from Tokyo to the sleepy country town of Yamagata and rediscovering hersel
 f in the process. Takahata renders these flashbacks in a style different f
 rom the present-day scenes—corners slightly fade into white\, edges blur
 —lending these moments a sense of impermanence. Though most Japanese ani
 me projects record dialogue after animation is finished\, this film revers
 ed much of that process\, allowing the visual artists to create more reali
 stic facial expressions. A surprise smash hit in Japan\, the film attracte
 d a largely adult audience with its poignant look at the cost of growing u
 p.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/only-yesterday-019dd4
 e5-382b-1b21-6b82-7f190efce69f
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The French Connection in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260615T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260615T223000
DTSTAMP:20260611T093549Z
UID:019dd56e-ab06-c1c3-3efe-ab5004739894@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, June 15\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum
  of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 44m\n\n1971 | 104 min. | USA | Color | 
 English | Rated R | 35mm \nDIRECTOR: William Friedkin \nWRITTEN BY: Erne
 st Tidyman  \nWITH: Gene Hackman\, Fernando Rey\, Roy Scheider\, Tony Lo 
 Bianco \nPrint courtesy of the Academy Film Archive.\n\nType: Screenings\
 n\nDirector William Friedkin helped usher in a new era of gritty police dr
 amas with this fact-based thriller about an unscrupulous New York cop (Gen
 e Hackman\, in a star-making\, Best Actor-winning performance) and his sid
 ekick (Roy Scheider) who face an international drug ring. A winner of five
  Oscars\, including Best Picture and Directing\, The French Connection set
  a high bar for documentary-inspired realism in commercial cinema while fe
 aturing one of the most exciting car-chase scenes of all time.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-french-connection
 -019dd56e-ab06-c1c3-3efe-ab5004739894
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Only Yesterday
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260617T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260617T150000
DTSTAMP:20260611T093549Z
UID:019dd4e5-ab29-acfb-eb7a-f52362fe8692@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Wednesday\, June 17\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Mus
 eum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 58m\n\n1991 | 118 min. | Japan | Col
 or | Japanese with English subtitles | Rated PG | DCP\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY
 : Isao Takahata \nWITH: Miki Imai\, Toshiro Yanagiba\, Yoko Honna\, Michi
 e Terada\n\nType: Screenings\n\nBased on the manga of the same name\, Isao
  Takahata’s second feature for Studio Ghibli is a serene memory piece fe
 aturing 27-year-old Taeko reminiscing about her 1960s childhood\, travelli
 ng from Tokyo to the sleepy country town of Yamagata and rediscovering her
 self in the process. Takahata renders these flashbacks in a style differen
 t from the present-day scenes—corners slightly fade into white\, edges b
 lur—lending these moments a sense of impermanence. Though most Japanese 
 anime projects record dialogue after animation is finished\, this film rev
 ersed much of that process\, allowing the visual artists to create more re
 alistic facial expressions. A surprise smash hit in Japan\, the film attra
 cted a largely adult audience with its poignant look at the cost of growin
 g up.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/only-yesterday-019dd4
 e5-ab29-acfb-eb7a-f52362fe8692
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Aardman Animations Celebration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260617T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260617T223000
DTSTAMP:20260611T093549Z
UID:019dd528-36b1-73cb-59ef-39c58d050ebc@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Selected by the Animation Branch\n\nWednesday\, June 17\, 2026
  at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1m\
 n\nAard Man \n1972 | 1 min | UK | Color | English \nDIRECTED BY: Peter Lor
 d\, David Sproxton \n\nCreature Comforts\n1990 | 5 min. | UK | Color | Eng
 lish \nDIRECTED BY: Nick Park \nWITH: Julie Sedgewick \n\nIdent \n1990 | 5
  min. | UK | Color | English \nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Richard Starzak \nWITH
 : Arthur Smith\, Phil Nice \n\nAdam  \n1992 | 6 min. | UK | Color | Engli
 sh \nDIRECTED BY: Peter Lord \nWITH: Nick Upton \n\nThe Wrong Trousers \n1
 993 | 30 min. | UK | Color | English \nDIRECTED BY: Nick Park \nWRITTEN BY
 : Nick Park\, Bob Baker\, Brian Sibley \nWITH: Peter Sallis \n\nHumdrum \n
 1999 | 7 min. | UK | Color | English \nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Peter Peake \n
 WITH: Moray Hunter\, Jack Docherty \n\nOff Beat \n2006 | 3 min. | UK | Col
 or | English\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Will Becher \nWITH: Michael Buerk \n\nR
 obin Robin \n2021 | 32 min. | UK | Color | English\nDIRECTED BY: Dan Ojari
 \, Mikey Please \nWRITTEN BY: Dan Ojari\, Mikey Please\, Sam Morrison \nWI
 TH: Bronte Carmichael\, Richard E. Grant\, Gillian Anderson\, Adeel Akhtar
 \n\nType: Screenings\n\nA selection of short films in celebration of the i
 nternationally acclaimed studio Aardman Animations. Aard Man was the first
  animated short (25 seconds long) produced by the studio. Creature Comfort
 s (1990 Animated Short Film winner) puts the voices and words of ordinary 
 Brits into the mouths of zoo animals. Ident (1990) tells the story of a cl
 ay-man and his changing relationship with the world around him. Adam (1992
  Animated Short Film nominee) takes an unusual look at the Biblical first 
 man. The Wrong Trousers (1993 Animated Short Film winner) pits Wallace and
  Gromit against a conniving penguin. Humdrum (1993 Animated Short Film nom
 inee) spotlights two bored silhouettes desperately looking for a way to li
 ven up their day. In Off Beat\, a man takes the opportunity of a police ho
 liday to attempt a crime. Robin Robin (2021 Animated Short nominee) tells 
 of a bird raised by mice.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/aardman-animations-50
 th-anniversary-019dd528-36b1-73cb-59ef-39c58d050ebc
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:10th Anniversary of Spa Night
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T210000
DTSTAMP:20260611T093549Z
UID:019de537-df5c-2aca-648c-405bd5af20d1@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: writer/director Andrew Ahn and actor Joe Seo\n\nThu
 rsday\, June 18\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pi
 ctures\n\nRuntime: 1h 33m\n\n2016 | 93 min | USA | Color | Korean\, Englis
 h\, Spanish | Unrated | DCP  \nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Andrew Ahn \nWITH: J
 oe Seo\, Haerry Kim\, Youn Ho Cho\, Tae Song\n\nType: Screenings\n\nAfter 
 high-school senior David Cho (Joe Seo) and his parents\, Soyoung and Jin (
 Haerry Kim\, Youn-Ho Cho)\, are forced to sell their family restaurant\, t
 hey take on odd jobs to get by. When his parents enroll David in expensive
  college prep courses\, he secretly takes a part-time job at a men’s jji
 mjilbang (bathhouse) to help with family finances. The choice also leads t
 o an unexpected awakening\, allowing David to explore his sexuality in a s
 pace reserved for illicit encounters. \nFilmmaker Andrew Ahn draws from hi
 s Korean American upbringing in the bustling Los Angeles neighborhood of K
 oreatown to capture a story about familial bonds and expectations\, explor
 ing the intersection of queer and cultural identity within the ongoing pur
 suit of the so-called American dream.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/spa-night-019de537-df
 5c-2aca-648c-405bd5af20d1
END:VEVENT
