UID:019e289e-6d6a-02c1-581e-1379f73b67b4@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Conversations
DESCRIPTION:Costume and textile conservator Melinda Kerstein and Icon Coll
 ection Co-Founder Bryan Johns explore the legacy of Marilyn Monroe through
  her iconic onscreen looks.\n\nFriday\, June 26\, 2026 at 12 pm\n\nLocatio
 n: Sidney Poitier Grand Lobby\n\nRuntime: 1h\n\nType: Conversations\n\nCos
 tume and textile conservator Melinda Kerstein and Icon Collection Co-Found
 er Bryan Johns explore the legacy of Marilyn Monroe through her iconic ons
 creen looks. \nAgainst the backdrop of the largest exhibition of Monroe's 
 onscreen costumes\, the conversation also delves into the late actress’s
  personal style and the many visual elements that came together to seal he
 r place among Hollywood legends. \nAssociate Curator Sophia Serrano modera
 tes.
