BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pom Poko
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T150000
DTSTAMP:20260611T093549Z
UID:019dd4f1-25a5-b1fa-e5e1-a3cc0af72ac7@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, June 26\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum
  of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 59m\n\n1994 | 119 min. | Japan | Color 
 | Japanese with English subtitles | Rated PG | DCP\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: I
 sao Takahata \nWITH: Shincho Kokontei\, Makoto Nonomura\, Yuriko Ishida\,
  Norihei Miki\n\nType: Screenings\n\nA motley band of tanuki—shapeshifti
 ng wild raccoon dogs—must battle humans to protect the idyllic Tama Hill
 s from being converted into a suburb. Isao Takahata’s epic is a playful 
 and entertaining adventure brimming with visual delights and surprises—t
 he film’s nocturnal spirit parade is a showstopper\, with many iconic ch
 aracters from other Studio Ghibli films\, including Kiki’s Delivery Serv
 ice and My Neighbor Totoro\, appearing in the sequence. A huge local hit t
 hat remains an under-screened gem in the Studio Ghibli catalog\, Pom Poko 
 infuses Japanese mythology with madcap energy\, bringing a light tone to h
 eavy topics such as gentrification and deforestation\, as the tanuki call 
 on their community to build a place where people can live in harmony despi
 te their differences.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/pom-poko-019dd4f1-25a
 5-b1fa-e5e1-a3cc0af72ac7
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Shadow of a Doubt with Guillermo del Toro
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T223000
DTSTAMP:20260611T093549Z
UID:019dda4f-bd35-37fa-baa8-c9a1d9017b86@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, June 26\, 2026 at 7 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of
  Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 48m\n\n1943 | 108 min. | USA | Black-and-W
 hite | English | 4K DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Alfred Hitchcock \nWRITTEN BY: Thor
 nton Wilder\, Sally Benson\, Alma Reville \nSTORY BY: Gordon McDonell \nWI
 TH: Teresa Wright\, Joseph Cotten\, MacDonald Carey\, Patricia Collinge\n\
 nType: Screenings\n\nDirector and lifelong Alfred Hitchcock fan Guillermo 
 del Toro delivers an in-depth lecture on this twisted family portrait from
  the Master of Suspense\, followed by a screening. \nThe date of this even
 t has moved to June 26. For questions or to request a refund\, email museu
 mtickets@oscars.org.\nShadow of a Doubt strikes an intimate noir tone\, an
 d features Teresa Wright as Charlotte “Young Charlie” Newton\, named a
 fter her favorite uncle\, Charles Oakley (Joseph Cotton). Set in the warm 
 and inviting town of Santa Rosa\, California\, where a strong sense of com
 munal security lingers in the air\, this psychological thriller surveys th
 e notion of human trust and its fragility through Charlotte’s growing su
 spicion of her uncle in the notorious Merry Widow murder case. The high-co
 ntrast lighting and meticulous application of shadows are woven in the sto
 rytelling\, elegantly orchestrated by the boldly framed static shots and d
 ramatic movements of the camera.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/shadow-of-a-doubt-wit
 h-guillermo-del-toro-019dda4f-bd35-37fa-baa8-c9a1d9017b86
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:There's No Business Like Show Business
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T223000
DTSTAMP:20260611T093549Z
UID:019dda69-eb64-242b-17a3-0f3f59a296b3@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, June 26\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum
  of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 57m\n\n1954 | 117 min | USA | Color | E
 nglish | Not Rated | DCP\nDIRECTED BY: Walter Lang \nWRITTEN BY: Phoebe E
 phron\, Henry Ephron \nWITH: Ethel Merman\, Donald O'Connor\, Marilyn Mon
 roe\, Dan Dailey\n\nType: Screenings\n\nThe Donahue clan\, led by husband 
 and wife Molly and Terry (Ethel Merman and Dan Dailey)\, navigate the ups 
 and downs of show biz\, from their beginnings in Vaudeville to the Great D
 epression\, in this musical comedy with songs by Irving Berlin. The family
 ’s close bond is further tested with the arrival of the talented and dri
 ven Vicky Parker (Marilyn Monroe). Costume designer Travilla played an int
 egral role in shaping Marilyn Monroe’s public image on- and off-screen. 
 Together they famously produced looks that evaded censorship while still c
 ourting controversy. His designs for her showgirl characters are of partic
 ular note.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/theres-no-business-li
 ke-show-business-019dda69-eb64-242b-17a3-0f3f59a296b3
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Goonies in 4K
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T121500
DTSTAMP:20260611T093549Z
UID:019dda33-4f68-ad1f-15d3-4abc0b61ec82@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Accessible screening\n\nSaturday\, June 27\, 2026 at 11 am\n\n
 Location: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 54m\n\n1985 | 1
 14 min. | USA | Color | Scope | English | Rated PG | 4K DCP  \nDIRECTED B
 Y: Richard Donner \nWRITTEN BY: Chris Columbus \nSTORY BY: Steven Spielb
 erg \nWITH: Sean Astin\, Josh Brolin\, Jeff Cohen\, Corey Feldman\n\nType
 : Screenings\n\nAccessible screeningOn the last Saturday of every month\, 
 the museum's Family Matinee is an accommodative screening where we offer o
 pen captioning\, keep the theater dimly lit\, and maintain a lower volume 
 specifically for neurodivergent viewers. \nHey\, you guys! Come join the G
 oonies\, a ragtag group of kids\, on a quest for lost pirate gold in this 
 classic 1980s adventure for the whole family. After finding an old map\, t
 he group\, led by Mikey (Sean Astin)\, sets off to find the long-lost trea
 sure of legendary pirate One-Eyed Willy\, in hopes of saving their family 
 homes from greedy developers. As the kids make their way through caves rig
 ged with boobytraps\, they are aided by the whimsical inventions of Data (
 future Oscar winner Ke Huy Quan) while avoiding the Fratellis\, a pair of 
 thieving brothers (Joe Pantoliano and Robert Davi) led by Mama Fratelli (t
 he inimitable Anne Ramsey) who plan to find the treasure themselves.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-goonies-019dda33-
 4f68-ad1f-15d3-4abc0b61ec82
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:North by Northwest with Guillermo del Toro
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T160000
DTSTAMP:20260611T093549Z
UID:019dda50-8ae2-01d8-d781-c585adaa77d1@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, June 27\, 2026 at 2 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum 
 of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 16m\n\n1959 | 136 min. | USA | Color | E
 nglish | 4K DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Alfred Hitchcock \nWRITTEN BY: Ernest Lehma
 n \nWITH: Cary Grant\, Eva Marie Saint\, James Mason\, Jessie Royce Landis
 \n\nType: Screenings\n\nDirector and lifelong Alfred Hitchcock fan Guiller
 mo del Toro delivers an in-depth lecture on this Cary Grant classic from t
 he Master of Suspense\, followed by a screening. \nThis event has been mo
 ved to June 27 at 2pm. For questions or to request a refund\, email museum
 tickets@oscars.org.\nHitchcock plays with a concept of the wrong man\, a f
 requent theme in his narratives\, in one of the most admired and entertain
 ing of his mid-career films. North by Northwest stars four-time collaborat
 or Grant as Roger O. Thornhill\, a suave ad executive whose identity is mi
 staken for a government agent. Ruthless spy Philip Vandamm (James Mason) i
 s after Thornhill\; on a separate mission is a group of secret agents who 
 follows Thornhill across the country. On the run\, Thornhill meets Eve Ken
 dall\, a mesmerizing\, peculiar woman whose mysterious identity amplifies 
 the level of danger he is in. The film’s ironically ecstatic tone parall
 els the enchanting aspect of Grant’s portrayal of Thornhill—elegantly 
 sarcastic with a witty sense of humor. Processed in Technicolor\, this spe
 ctacular thriller showcases now-iconic action sequences such as the crop d
 uster plane chase and climax at Mount Rushmore.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/north-by-northwest-wi
 th-guillermo-del-toro-019dda50-8ae2-01d8-d781-c585adaa77d1
END:VEVENT
