UID:019dda60-0589-9655-e49d-f0fa19d1ec52@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, June 28\, 2026 at 3 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of
  Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 59m\n\n1960 | 119 min | USA | Color | Engl
 ish | Not Rated | DCP\nDIRECTED BY: George Cukor  \nWRITTEN BY: Norman K
 rasna \nWITH: Marilyn Monroe\, Yves Montand\, Tony Randall\, Frankie Vaug
 han\n\nType: Screenings\n\nDirector George Cukor’s musical comedy was Mo
 nroe’s second-to-last completed film. She plays a bohemian off-Broadway 
 actor who is in a show satirizing a French billionaire\, Jean-Marc Clémen
 t (Yves Montand). While scoping out the production\, Clément is cast in t
 he play and the two fall in love\, though deception threatens to ruin ever
 ything. Monroe worked closely with costume designer Dorothy Jeakins to dra
 w inspiration from her personal style for the film’s looks.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/lets-make-love-019dda
 60-0589-9655-e49d-f0fa19d1ec52
