 : Isao Takahata \nWITH: Yukiji Asaoka\, Toru Masuoka\, Masako Araki\, Hay
 ato Isohata\n\nType: Screenings\n\nIsao Takahata’s adaptation of Hisaich
 i Ishii’s beloved slice-of-life manga departs from Studio Ghibli’s tra
 ditional anime style and instead uses a roughly sketched comic-strip look.
  Awash in pastel watercolors\, My Neighbors the Yamadas delights in the ev
 eryday misadventures of its titular family—dad\, mom\, older brother\, l
 ittle sister\, granny\, and Pochi the dog. Punctuated by daydreams and fan
 tasies\, Takahata’s film is a heart-warming and honest look at modern fa
 mily life. Along with its typical animation style\, Ghibli forgoes its usu
 al long\, orchestral music in favor of short piano themes to match its epi
 sodic style\, making the film a standout in the studio’s filmography.
