BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Downhill Racer in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260722T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260722T223000
DTSTAMP:20260611T093549Z
UID:019dd530-50e1-a2f7-0398-9b2968ece910@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Selected by the Directors Branch\n\nWednesday\, July 22\, 2026
  at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 
 41m\n\n1969 | 101 min. | USA | Color | English/German/French | Rated PG | 
 35mm \nDIRECTED BY: Michael Ritchie \nWRITTEN BY: James Salter \nWITH: Rob
 ert Redford\, Gene Hackman\, Camilla Sparv\, Joe Jay Jalbert \n35mm print 
 courtesy of Paramount Pictures Archive.\n\nType: Screenings\n\nRobert Redf
 ord used the clout from the success of Butch Cassidy and the Sundance Kid
 —and his personal obsession with winter sports—to spearhead this chara
 cter study set in the international world of downhill skiing. Redford play
 s David Chappellet\, a talented athlete for whom relationships are seconda
 ry to his drive to compete. Michael Ritchie made his impressive directoria
 l feature debut with this atypical sports drama\, filming his actors at au
 thentic skiing events. Ritchie’s later three decades demonstrated his ap
 titude in a wide variety of genres and included classics such as the origi
 nal The Bad News Bears (1976) and the Oscar-winning political satire The C
 andidate (1972)\, which reunited him with Redford.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/downhill-racer-019dd5
 30-50e1-a2f7-0398-9b2968ece910
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cape Fear (1962) in 4K
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260723T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260723T223000
DTSTAMP:20260611T093549Z
UID:019dd581-d2bc-67e5-c083-4b3ad7f2a472@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Thursday\, July 23\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Muse
 um of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 45m\n\n1962 | 105 min. | USA | Black-
 and-White | English | Not Rated | 4K DCP \nDIRECTED BY: J. Lee Thompson \
 nWRITTEN BY: James R. Webb \nWITH: Gregory Peck\, Robert Mitchum\, Polly 
 Bergen\, Lori Martin\n\nType: Screenings\n\nBased on the 1957 novel The Ex
 ecutioners and produced by Gergory Peck’s Melville Productions\, J. Lee 
 Thompson’s Cape Fear broke new ground with audiences and pushed the limi
 ts of on-screen terror. Criminal attorney Sam Bowden (Gregory Peck) become
 s the target of the unhinged Max Cady (Robert Mitchum)\, a recently releas
 ed criminal who blames Bowden for his imprisonment. Bowden’s worst fears
  come true when Cady begins to harass and threaten Bowden’s wife and dau
 ghter\, forcing him to take matters into his own hands in a pulse-pounding
  climax backed by a Bernard Herrmann score.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/cape-fear-1962-019dd5
 81-d2bc-67e5-c083-4b3ad7f2a472
END:VEVENT
