SUMMARY:Who Framed Roger Rabbit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T121500
DTSTAMP:20260611T093549Z
UID:019db102-6a44-5086-0897-939caa28feba@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, August 1\, 2026 at 11 am\n\nLocation: Academy Museu
 m of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 47m\n\n1988. 107 min. USA. Color. Engl
 ish. Rated PG. DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Robert Zemeckis  \nWRITTEN BY: Jeffrey
  Price\, Peter S. Seaman \nWITH: Bob Hoskins\, Christopher Lloyd\, Joanna
  Cassidy\, Charles Fleischer\n\nType: Screenings\n\nEddie Valiant (Bob Hos
 kins)\, a private eye in 1930s Los Angeles\, gets an unexpected client—R
 oger Rabbit\, a cartoon film star. Director Robert Zemeckis’s witty come
 dy-mystery is a dazzling mix of live-action and animation\, incorporating 
 beloved cartoon characters from Disney and other studios. Nominated for it
 s art direction\, cinematography\, and sound\, it won for its film editing
 \, sound effects editing\, and visual effects. Richard Williams also recei
 ved a Special Achievement Award from the Academy for his animation directi
 on.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/who-framed-roger-rabb
 it-019db102-6a44-5086-0897-939caa28feba
