 seum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 15m\n\n2002 | 75 min. | Japan | Col
 or | Japanese with English subtitles | Rated G | DCP\nDIRECTED BY: Hiroyuk
 i Morita \nWRITTEN BY: Reiko Yoshida \nWITH: Chizuru Ikewaki\, Yoshihiko
  Hakamada\, Aki Maeda\, Takayuki Yamada\n\nType: Screenings\n\nA spin-off 
 of Whisper of the Heart\, The Cat Returns finds another schoolgirl encount
 ering a mysterious tomcat on the street\, though this time she is led to a
  fantastic world beyond her wildest dreams. Launched into a cobblestoned m
 agic kingdom ruled by cat royalty—including a motorcade replete with vas
 sals\, maidens\, and even Secret Service—she must enlist the help of the
  elusive Baron Humbert von Gikkingen (the same cat featured as a statue in
  Whisper of the Heart) if she hopes to make it back home. The only feature
