SUMMARY:Howl’s Moving Castle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260810T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260810T150000
DTSTAMP:20260611T093549Z
UID:019dd51d-7564-f197-c616-12ecc8530357@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, August 10\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Muse
 um of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 59m\n\n2004 | 119 min. | Japan | Colo
 r | Japanese with English subtitles | Rated PG | DCP\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY:
  Hayao Miyazaki \nWITH: Chieko Baisho\, Takuya Kimura\, Akihiro Miwa\, Ta
 tsuya Gashûin\n\nType: Screenings\n\nAn adaptation of Diana Wynne Jones
 ’s fantasy novel of the same name\, the Oscar-nominated Howl’s Moving 
 Castle is a pitch-perfect fairy tale about aging and war\, set in a dazzli
 ng steampunk world. When young hatmaker Sophie is transformed into a 90-ye
 ar-old woman by the vengeful Witch of the Waste\, she seeks to break the c
 urse with the help of the enigmatic wizard Howl\, the fire demon Calcifer\
 , and the magical moving castle they inhabit.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/howls-moving-castle-0
 19dd51d-7564-f197-c616-12ecc8530357
